+# Add #2590 to the explicit auto-ID co-repair
+
+Prepared from `dbdbb05a407b4ff10a6bfc0587a3bc9133ac29b9` with the v10 credit-cap removal intact. This appends four exact #2590 regressions and one genuine control to #1002; all former nine regressions, two controls, baseline/environment/scope fields and review obligations remain unchanged. The other twenty-seven contracts are unchanged.
+
+## The v10 failure is real overlap
+
+Candidate `33fbf17558062276c223946b66aa3f7c01810ad6` moved ID copy-back inside the engine transaction. Its previous eleven focused cases passed. #2590 InsertOne still throws InvalidCastException, but its hidden durable ObjectId row and byte-change failures disappear because the transaction now rolls back. Restoring the old fingerprint would restore a defect. The other three #2590 paths already rolled back and still fail their wrong diagnostic. All four cases must be repaired explicitly.
+
+Preserve the paused v10 campaign, consumed attempt, worker [35075342165](https://github.com/litedb-org/LiteDB/actions/runs/35075342165) and failed CI [35077204440](https://github.com/litedb-org/LiteDB/actions/runs/35077204440). The old candidate is unaccepted implementation input. A new immutable contract/runtime and superseding campaign must retain the integrated base `bbb0253bc06324f0bb14a21a727a37e8c7f2b213`, export the complete repaired patch, run fresh compressed CI and obtain all three reviews. No unchanged-candidate CI rerun can make the four remaining failures green.
+
+The fixer-only task note identifies the exact seed commit, Insert.cs path, source branch, worker/CI runs and git-show command. It expressly forbids treating the seed as accepted base. This reuses implementation work without rewriting the old state or adding a controller seed feature.
+
+## Evidence and exact scope
+
+[issue-1002-2811-2590-corepair.json](../../../scripts/bugfix/fixtures/issue-1002-2811-2590-corepair.json) retains the previous contract, new contract, all sixteen exact names/IDs/classes/outcomes, full canonical failures, representative raw failures and the twelve original baseline/repeat report pins. All sixteen selections match across original six-lane run34988724926 and its unrelated repeat candidate, plus both net8/net10 v10 integration baselines: **fourteen baseline gates passed**. Both v10 candidates remain rejected with exactly four failed targets. Their source/workflow/test SHAs and actual x64 testhost identities were verified locally.
+
+The existing normalization policy is unchanged. It already replaces the single generated ObjectId in the original #2590 InsertOne failure, with exact required match count one; the rest of the full diagnostic—including hidden row and byte-change assertions—is hash-bound. No changed failure or source guard is allowed.
+
+New frozen source: `LiteDB.Tests/Issues/Issue2590_Tests.cs`, blob `76cb4f55627ffccee1a6eb77753931a3786493fb`, from original `dd937719f7eee53c512f50ac604cab639bf42a4c`. The AutoId_Tests control file was already frozen. Production scope remains only `LiteDB/Client/Database/Collections/Insert.cs`; the shared helpers serve single/enumerable Insert, InsertBulk and Upsert. Existing Ubuntu net8/net10, production-build and compatibility requirements remain unchanged. No credit-cap, worker, controller, normalization, frozen-test or production file is edited.
+
+| New regression suffix | Test ID | Original full failure SHA-256 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| InsertMany | `ff0e12e0-2217-2965-fd57-0b1f33952c14` | `d27dd3fd3a45430331874bb58efe26ed78a78850b53e8950a46359e174ac2e43` |
+| InsertOne | `1aae9c09-e5c5-f11a-0c6a-38f1dfe0b917` | `a5cb127e80308bbf3f4f3782a83988986973b0e73c564001af1e594e30427fa7` |
+| UpsertMany | `78c16fad-1f1e-9414-a924-65cc79f7b55b` | `d27dd3fd3a45430331874bb58efe26ed78a78850b53e8950a46359e174ac2e43` |
+| UpsertOne | `3b58fea5-5574-4b86-bf26-367daae865ca` | `d27dd3fd3a45430331874bb58efe26ed78a78850b53e8950a46359e174ac2e43` |
+
+All four belong to `LiteDB.Tests.Issues.Issue2590_Tests.Empty_string_ids_are_addressable_or_rejected_before_any_write`. The new positive control is `LiteDB.Tests.Database.AutoId_Tests.AutoId_BsonDocument`, ID `ec5e0f64-4e16-3ded-3f46-9836fa12f2ea`. It actually inserts an untyped generated ObjectId and explicit Int32 key and queries their documents. The existing AutoId_Strong_Typed control covers writable typed IDs and nonempty String IDs. Both pass every original/repeat/current baseline report.
+
+## Required behavior
+
+Reject the unsupported generated ObjectId-to-String member assignment before writes with `LiteException.DATA_TYPE_NOT_ASSIGNABLE` (214), exactly `Data type System.String is not assignable from data type LiteDB.ObjectId`. Do not introduce string auto-ID support or catch/relabel the failure after writing. On rejection, #2590 checks the entire original String/ObjectId ledger, byte-identical file and unchanged empty target IDs across all four API paths.
+
+Preserve assigned nonempty strings, including 24-hex-character strings as String keys distinct from ObjectId keys; explicit-ID overloads; custom member mapping; untyped BsonDocument generation; and existing nullable/writable numeric behavior. All former get-only nullable-ID, throwing-setter, explicit transaction/caller Commit, mixed/lazy batch and compatibility obligations remain in task.json.
+
+New additive role instructions:
+
+- **behavior**: This additive co-repair includes all four frozen #2590 String/ObjectId auto-ID cases. Reject an unsupported generated ObjectId assignment to a String ID before any write with LiteException.DATA_TYPE_NOT_ASSIGNABLE (214) and exactly: Data type System.String is not assignable from data type LiteDB.ObjectId. Do not merely catch or relabel InvalidCastException after a write, restore a hidden durable row to preserve the old failure, or invent new string auto-ID support as part of this bounded repair. All thirteen regressions and three controls must pass.
+- **behavior**: For the fixer: Unaccepted implementation seed only: prior candidate 33fbf17558062276c223946b66aa3f7c01810ad6 from fix/issue-1002-hosted-v10-1002-a1, produced by run 35075342165, failed combined CI 35077204440. Inspect git show 33fbf17558062276c223946b66aa3f7c01810ad6:LiteDB/Client/Database/Collections/Insert.cs to reuse and improve its transactional copy-back design. Keep HEAD and the accepted base at bbb0253bc06324f0bb14a21a727a37e8c7f2b213, and export the complete new patch relative to that base. The seed passed the former eleven focused cases but all four #2590 cases still failed; it is not accepted and its checks do not substitute for fresh CI or reviews. Preserve the consumed v10 attempt and failed history under the explicit superseding campaign.
+- **compatibility**: For #2590 preserve assigned nonempty String IDs, including 24-hex-character strings distinct from ObjectId keys, explicit-ID overloads and custom mapper/member configuration. AutoId_Strong_Typed independently covers assigned String and writable typed IDs; AutoId_BsonDocument independently covers untyped ObjectId auto-generation and explicit Int32 keys. Reject only the unsupported generated-value/member-type combination; do not block BsonDocument or existing correctly assignable mappings. Preserve all prior persisted key, sequence, reopen and upgrade compatibility obligations.
+- **lifecycle**: For #2590 verify pre-write rejection leaves the complete original String/ObjectId control ledger, file bytes and target empty String IDs unchanged across InsertOne, InsertMany, UpsertOne and UpsertMany. Keep assignment inside the transaction for all newly reachable throwing setters; the v10 removal of hidden-row/byte-change assertions was a real atomicity improvement, not diagnostic drift. Retain all earlier get-only nullable-ID, explicit transaction, caller Commit, lazy/mixed batch and non-null throwing-setter evidence requirements.
+
+## Preparation checks
+
+New adversarial tests cover all thirteen red/three green cases, exact full failures and identities, the rejected v10 seed, unchanged former case lists/requirements, missing/skipped/extra cases, partial repairs and unrelated source-guard passes. Historical nine-regression proof remains separately tested; the test-only preservation helper permits only the digest-pinned additive contract. Fresh hosted validation and three reviews remain required after implementation.
+
+Validation completed: **14 actual baseline replays and 27 focused checks passed** (7 expanded gate, 8 profile/delivery, 7 historical co-repair, 5 preservation checks). Both authenticated v10 candidates remain rejected. No full-suite or CI rerun was launched for preparation.
